; A binding name smuggled in via a string identifier must not start with
; `_` — a local '_rp' would shadow the internal caller-page slot exactly
; the way a plain `rp` binding did before the slot was renamed. Normal
; identifiers cannot start with `_` (lexer); this closes the freeform-
; identifier hole.
; xfail: binding names must not start with _
var v Vector[int](4)
let '_rp' v.data
print("unreachable")
